FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:1985 — `edge_the_delivery_rule_covers_each_phase_in_flight_and_no_other` iterates `DELIVERY_SUBJECT_PREFIXES` itself and feeds each entry back through `scan`, so it verifies only that whatever is in the list is honoured; it never asserts which phases must be in it. Deleting an entry (e.g. `"resume phase-073:"`, the phase under review) leaves this test green. The only other tests that name a concrete prefix are `edge_a_rebuilt_delivery_commit_is_neither_unreviewed_nor_stale` (phase-088) and `edge_a_delivery_subject_of_another_phase_is_not_acknowledged_by_the_rule` (phase-083, asserting absence), and `edge_the_delivery_commit_is_acknowledged_by_the_rule_and_by_no_entry:2033` only requires the list to match *some* commit, so one surviving prefix satisfies it. The per-phase coverage the change claims to add is therefore unpinned. Fix: assert the exact expected prefix set (`assert_eq!` against a hardcoded list) or hardcode each in-flight prefix, including `"resume phase-073:"`, in a dedicated test.

2. [MINOR] tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:1955 — `edge_the_phase_under_review_delivery_is_acknowledged_by_subject_not_a_stale_sha` does `let Some(phase) = delivery_phase(subject) else { return; };`, so when HEAD's subject is not a `resume phase-NNN:` shape the test passes without a single assertion. That is the only test that would catch removal of the phase's own prefix when HEAD happens to be a delivery commit, and it silently asserts nothing otherwise. Fix: assert unconditionally that `DELIVERY_SUBJECT_PREFIXES` contains `"resume phase-073:"`, or drive the check from a synthetic `resume phase-073: adopt preserved work` log line rather than from HEAD.

3. [STYLE] tests/bench/mod.rs:22 — `unicode_width` is pulled in as a normal `[dependencies]` entry (Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock) although only the `tests/bench` harness uses it; that expands the shipped library/wasm dependency graph for a table-formatting helper, and the project already has cell-width logic in `src/error.rs` (per the phase-059 acknowledgement entry). Consider reusing that helper or gating the crate to the harness, and confirm the library/wasm targets do not acquire it. Not a runtime defect; noting it because the REPORT frames the phase as test-only.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 3
